 <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:03:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/30] metal: exact ducc0 parity on real data (float64 coords,
 wrap, odd anchor)

Three measurement-found discrepancies, all from imaging real LOFAR data
through -mgpu (synthetic probes never exercised these regimes):

1. float32 cell coordinates quantise the sub-cell fraction to ulp(cell)
   (6e-5 at 784 cells, 1e-3 at 15000): split into integer base + [0,1)
   fraction on the CPU in double, 6 floats per visibility.
2. ducc0 wraps out-of-grid visibilities into the grid (getpix frac);
   we culled them (23% of LOFAR rows): wrap centred coords mod grid on
   the CPU, wrap taps mod grid in every kernel (matches ducc0 dump()).
3. Odd-support tap window: poly wrote 6 taps for W=7 (missing the -3 tap)
   and anchored on floor where ducc0 anchors round-half-up (iu0 =
   floor(u - supp/2 + 1)); base is now round-half-up for odd support,
   floor for even (exact there).

Real LOFAR 3C196 dirty via -mgpu: T2 rel_rms 3.6e-03 -> 4.6e-06
(limit 1e-4). Synthetic w-sweep: 1.28e-05 -> 1.5e-07. Single-vis:
2.6e-04 -> 3e-07.

